  "limitations": [
    "B2 is a single source-locked 5,528-byte zero-relocation gfx950 gpuReadWrite case with a fixed descriptor, OLD_ABI kernarg offsets, queue geometry, 19-PC sequence, and functional oracle. It is not a generic gfx950 compatibility claim, arbitrary HSACO loader, relocation proof, or broad operator suite.",
    "The 304 lifecycle records are instruction-start events. The independent CU numInstrExecuted=304 stat and 16 completed-wave stat prove execution of this locked run, but B2 does not expose or claim a separate per-instruction retirement trace.",
    "CPU-less means the generated runtime object graph has no CPU, Process, Ruby, TLB, HSAPP, GPUCommandProcessor, or AMDGPUDevice object. The physical host and ELF are x86-64, and gem5's monolithic library still links generic BaseCPU/System symbols that are not instantiated by this config.",
    "The host-native CU path is functional and accepts only the locked plain read/write traffic; atomics and unsupported memory commands are rejected. General barriers, fences, atomics, scratch/LDS, translation, Ruby coherence, timing accuracy, and arbitrary instruction semantics are not established.",
    "The direct-u64 completion signal is the bounded native B2 layout, not a proof of legacy amd_signal_t layout, complete HSA runtime signal semantics, or a transparent HIP/OpenCL launcher.",
    "The five host-native checkers and eight VEGA_X86 binaries are regression evidence. Their standalone boundaries do not independently prove B2 execution; the hash-pinned B2 run, output oracle, stats, and object graph provide that evidence.",
    "Qwen3.5-0.8B remains offline model-integrity and 15/15 static-contract evidence. Triton end-to-end and Qwen inference remain 0/1; CPU or NVIDIA execution is not an AMD pass. Full ROCm/OpenCL CTS, hardware, timing, throughput, latency, power, and performance claims remain outside scope.",
    "This detailed evidence binds the renewed frozen dirty-tree source inventory and exact pre/post-run ELF, not the final clean gem5 child commit/tree. The coordinator must bind the eventual child identity in a separate umbrella manifest."
  ],
